{
  "_id": "6ad0c4339a0ea1f99f78c273",
  "Package": "mixeff",
  "Title": "Mixed-Effects Models via the 'mixeff-rs' Rust Crate",
  "Version": "0.2.0",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(\"Brad\", \"Buchsbaum\",\nemail = \"brad.buchsbaum@gmail.com\",\nrole = c(\"aut\", \"cre\", \"cph\"),\ncomment = \"author of mixeff and the bundled 'mixeff-rs' crate\"),\nperson(\"Authors of the dependency Rust crates\",\nrole = \"ctb\",\ncomment = \"see inst/AUTHORS for details\"))",
  "Copyright": "file inst/COPYRIGHTS",
  "Description": "Fits linear and generalized linear mixed-effects models\nfrom 'lme4'-style formulas, with optimization by the bundled\n'mixeff-rs' Rust crate. A fitted model stores the compiled\nmodel specification, the optimizer certificate, and\nper-coefficient inference metadata (method, status,\nreliability) as data, so a result can be inspected, saved, and\nreloaded without a live handle to the compiled engine. When an\ninference method is unavailable for a fit, the affected value\nis either withheld with a stable reason code or reported under\nthe name of the method actually used, never silently swapped.\nVignettes cover migration from 'lme4' and the meaning of\nrandom-effects formula syntax.",
  "License": "MIT + file LICENSE",
  "URL": "https://bbuchsbaum.github.io/mixeff/,\nhttps://github.com/bbuchsbaum/mixeff",
